  "ended_on_llm_error": true,
  "final_message": "<think>Excellent \u2014 all frontend interactions work. Now let me add the smoke test script to package.json as \"test\": \"node tests/smoke.mjs\" so it can be run easily. And add a build+test ordering note.\n\nAlso, I should double check the \"Use my location\" success path (with coordinates) \u2014 the plot should show the visitor and the list should show distances. Let me add that to the smoke test: after the denied test, redefine geolocation to succeed with coordinates and check that the request includes lat/lng/radius and that the store list shows \"km away\" and the plot shows \"You are here\".\n\nThe stub returns stores with distance_km: null though. Let me make the stub compute distance_km when lat/lng are present: if the URL contains \"lat=\", return stores with distance_km set. That better mimics the API.\n\nLet me update the stub:\n```js\nif (path.startsWith(\"/api/stores\")) {\n  const url = new URL(path, \"http://localhost\");\n  const lat = url.searchParams.get(\"lat\");\n  const lng = url.searchParams.get(\"lng\");\n  const radius = url.searchParams.get(\"radius\");\n  let items = stores;\n  if (lat && lng) {\n    items = stores.map(s => ({...s, distance_km: Math.round(Math.hypot(s.latitude-lat, s.longitude-lng)*100)/100}));\n    if (radius) items = items.filter(s => s.distance_km <= Number(radius));\n  }\n  return jsonResponse({items});\n}\n```\n\nThen the location success test: geolocation returns coords (52.52, 13.405), radius default 10 \u2192 request \"/api/stores?lat=52.52&lng=13.405&radius=10\" \u2192 items with distance_km \u2192 the UI shows \"km away\" and the plot shows \"You are here\".\n\nLet me add that.\n\nAlso I want to test the radius selector change \u2192 request with the new radius.\n\nLet me update the test.</think>\n\n",
